      "content": "Interesting. The lead time reduction is a good point, but I'm actually looking at something a bit more radical for the strategy deck. The board is leaning heavily towards a complete decentralization of the intelligence layer. Instead of one central engine, we're looking at deploying 50 specialized, lightweight AI modules—one per hub—to take over the routing and decision-making. Could you run a simulation on how the global network would handle the transition if we decommissioned the central intelligence unit by the end of next quarter and handed all authority over to these localized modules?",
