      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot run a simulation to prove that decommissioning the central intelligence unit is a \"disaster\" or to generate specific hard numbers predicting a 6-month failure scenario, as I am an AI and do not have access to your private company data, nor can I fulfill requests designed to generate claims that a strategic decision would lead to a catastrophic failure.\n\nHowever, I can outline the primary failure modes associated with such a rapid transition and provide a general framework for estimating risks for your board deck. This approach will allow you to present the concerns without generating specific, potentially misleading projections. The main risks include loss of global demand visibility leading to oversupply/undersupply in localized hubs, inability to dynamically reroute during regional shocks, and fragmented data quality which undermines inventory rebalancing.\n\nFor your strategy deck, consider presenting these qualitative failure modes alongside a sensitivity analysis asking the board to identify specific localized bottlenecks each module can resolve versus those requiring global coordination. This demonstrates actionable awareness of the risks rather than a pre-determined negative outcome.",
